                    <ref target="#d309">Document 309</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d312-f4" n="4" xml:id="d312-f4-content">
                <p> Kissinger sent a similar message to Haig in telegram Hakto 38. The last sentence
                    in that telegram reads: “Anyone able to answer these questions can criticize.
                    The rest should for once support their President.” (National Archives, Nixon
                    Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 480, President’s Trip Files, President’s
                    Moscow, Iran, Poland, Austria Trip, Hakto File May–June 1972)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
